<#task-12-pin-refetch-after-failure> a plan:Task;
    dct:title "Pin pos-resource re-fetch after a failed fetch via a proper test";
    plan:touchesFile "core/src/Store.spec.ts", "elements/src/components/pos-resource/pos-resource.integration.spec.tsx";
    plan:dependsOn <#task-09-drop-store-force-fetch>;
    plan:parent <#plan>;
    dct:created "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date;
    plan:note <#entry-task-12-pin-refetch-after-failure-note-01>;
    plan:option <#entry-task-12-pin-refetch-after-failure-option-03>, <#entry-task-12-pin-refetch-after-failure-option-02>, <#entry-task-12-pin-refetch-after-failure-option-01>;
    plan:context <#entry-task-12-pin-refetch-after-failure-context-01>;
    plan:goal <#entry-task-12-pin-refetch-after-failure-goal-01>.
<#entry-task-12-pin-refetch-after-failure-note-01> a schema:Comment;
    schema:text "Verified against rdflib 2.4.1 source: HTTP failures >= 400 are never auto-retried; handleError's credentials-retry only fires for credentials 'include' (PodOS uses 'omit'), and the proxy retry needs a configured crossSiteProxy. So there is no hidden retry path the test could exploit — the session boundary is the only lever without touching implementation.";
    prov:wasAttributedTo <../agents.ttl#llm-glm-5.3-flash>;
    dct:created "2026-10-20T18:58:00Z"^^xsd:dateTime.
<#entry-task-12-pin-refetch-after-failure-option-03> a schema:Comment;
    schema:text "Option C — REJECTED: re-introduce force: true in Store.fetch (only when the document is in 'fetched'/'failed' state). Contradicts task-09 decision-02, and Angelo ruled the fix must come from a test, not the implementation.";
    prov:wasAttributedTo <../agents.ttl#llm-glm-5.3-flash>;
    dct:created "2026-10-20T18:58:00Z"^^xsd:dateTime.
<#entry-task-12-pin-refetch-after-failure-option-02> a schema:Comment;
    schema:text "Option B — cheap core-level pin: Store.spec test proving flagAuthorizationMetadata() enables re-fetching a previously failed document (probe already proved it green: 1 network call after the 404, 2 after the flag). Does not green the integration test by itself but pins the mechanism in core; combinable with Option A.";
    prov:wasAttributedTo <../agents.ttl#llm-glm-5.3-flash>;
    dct:created "2026-10-20T18:58:00Z"^^xsd:dateTime.
<#entry-task-12-pin-refetch-after-failure-option-01> a schema:Comment;
    schema:text "Option A — session boundary via the real login flow: mock notFound(..., {once:true}) plus turtleFile(..., {once:true}); render pos-app with pos-login and the pos-resource; after the error shows, drive pos-login's Login button with the authenticatedUser() OIDC mock (pattern from pos-login.integration.spec). The session emission makes PodOS's tap call flagAuthorizationMetadata(), which un-flags the failed response; the subsequent resource.fetch() then hits MSW and the label renders. Most realistic, no prod-code change.";
    prov:wasAttributedTo <../agents.ttl#llm-glm-5.3-flash>;
    dct:created "2026-10-20T18:58:00Z"^^xsd:dateTime.
<#entry-task-12-pin-refetch-after-failure-context-01> a schema:Comment;
    schema:text "Since dropping force: true (task-09), a failed rdflib load() is recorded (fetcher.requested[docuri] = status, nonexistent flags) and replayed as a dummy error response on every later load() of the same document. Only passing force: true or flagging the recorded response outOfDate (what PodOS's session tap does via flagAuthorizationMetadata()) re-enables an actual network fetch. A plain second resource.fetch() therefore cannot work — the test must trigger the session boundary.";
    prov:wasAttributedTo <../agents.ttl#llm-glm-5.3-flash>;
    dct:created "2026-10-20T18:58:00Z"^^xsd:dateTime.
<#entry-task-12-pin-refetch-after-failure-goal-01> a schema:Comment;
    schema:text "The red integration test 'replaces the error with the label when a subsequent fetch succeeds' goes green again by driving the re-fetch through a real invalidation path in the test — without changing any implementation code.";
    prov:wasAttributedTo <../agents.ttl#llm-glm-5.3-flash>;
    dct:created "2026-10-20T18:58:00Z"^^xsd:dateTime.
<#task-09-drop-store-force-fetch> dct:title "Drop Store.fetch force: true, rely on session-boundary invalidation".
<#entry-task-09-drop-store-force-fetch-context-01> schema:text "Surfaced while reviewing the task-08 gateway profile fetch (2026-10-19): Store.fetch forces every request; caching belongs at the rdflib/Store level, not in gateways. Originally drafted as 'keep force, add session-boundary invalidation'; flipped to 'drop force now' after Angelo pointed out rdflib 2.4.1 already carries the PR #871 fix (decision-02).".
<#entry-task-09-drop-store-force-fetch-goal-01> schema:text "Store.fetch() no longer force-fetches every request: drop force: true; rdflib's fetcher state is invalidated at the session boundary via the session tap's flagAuthorizationMetadata(). Re-fetching happens when the session changes, not on every fetch.".
