<#entry-task-08-review-fixes-search-demand-api-openQuestion-01> a schema:Comment;
    schema:text "[REMOVED 2026-10-19] Open question: should SearchGateway.buildSearchIndex fetch the profile itself, given it is normally already fetched after login (redundant) but without a hard guarantee when core is used standalone? The question is resolved — the fetch stays as-is, recorded in decision-01 — so the plan:openQuestion assertion was removed; this history lives here.";
    prov:wasAttributedTo <https://angelo.veltens.org/profile/card#me>;
    dct:created "2026-10-19T19:54:03Z"^^xsd:dateTime.
<#entry-task-08-review-fixes-search-demand-api-note-03> a schema:Comment;
    schema:text "Resolution of the apparent conflict between review scope-01 (drop the logged-out clear() added by ab0e358a) and that commit's message (\"the gateway owns the lifecycle and must be self-consistent\"): the reviewer is right. Angelo ruled that a gateway in PodOS will never be used without a PodOS instance — the PodOS instance is crucial for everything — so the standalone-gateway scenario the commit defended against cannot occur; PodOS's session tap fires on every session emission and clears before any subsequent demand call, making the in-branch clear() redundant. Rejected (LLM-proposed, not taken up): moving the session subscription into SearchGateway to make the gateway the literal single owner — the tap stays in PodOS and the branch clear is dropped in task-08 as scoped.";
    prov:wasAttributedTo <https://angelo.veltens.org/profile/card#me>;
    dct:created "2026-10-19T20:04:16Z"^^xsd:dateTime.
