<#entry-task-09-drop-store-force-fetch-decision-02> a schema:Comment;
    prov:wasAttributedTo <https://angelo.veltens.org/profile/card#me>;
    dct:created "2026-10-19T22:02:13Z"^^xsd:dateTime.
<#entry-task-09-drop-store-force-fetch-note-05> schema:text "Angelo caught the process gap (2026-10-20): the describedby de-force shipped as a refactor with no test pinning it, and the PodOs session-boundary test cannot be shown red independently. He kept the guard test (accepted as a pin rather than a red-green driver) and ruled that a negative test pinning the absence of force: true is overkill — the describedby de-force stays unpinned by design.".
<#entry-task-09-drop-store-force-fetch-verification-01> schema:text "Store.spec: 'serves an already fetched document from the store without re-fetching it' proved red (2 calls before the drop) and drives force: true's removal; describedby metadata load de-forced in a follow-up refactor, whole core suite green (431 tests) and typecheck clean after each step. PodOs.spec 'session boundary' guard pins that a session change re-fetches an already loaded document (proven green only against the full stack — the guard cannot be shown red independently since force: true also covered this path).".
<#entry-task-09-drop-store-force-fetch-note-01> schema:text "Dropping force does not reintroduce auth-error caching: non-forced load() re-fetches every failure state except 404 (verified against rdflib 2.4.1).".
<#entry-task-09-drop-store-force-fetch-note-02> schema:text "rdflib 2.4.1 (core's actual version) already contains the upstream PR #871 fix; flagAuthorizationMetadata() in the session tap is a working invalidation boundary — earlier research read a stale rdflib 2.3.2 copy, which produced the wrong conclusion behind the superseded decision-01.".
<#entry-task-09-drop-store-force-fetch-note-03> schema:text "RESOLVED during implementation (2026-10-20): without force, a repeated load is answered by rdflib's dedup with the original response — headers intact — so the offline cache is unaffected. Pinned by OfflineCapableFetcher.spec 'puts data to cache when rdflib dedups a repeated load'.".
<#entry-task-09-drop-store-force-fetch-note-04> schema:text "pos-app fetches the profile before consumers' session watches fire, so the demand-build re-download disappears for that flow; call sites of store.fetch/fetchAll: Store.ts (describedby), ProfileGateway, SearchGateway.fetchAll.".
<#entry-task-09-drop-store-force-fetch-openQuestion-01> schema:text "[REMOVED 2026-10-19] Resolved by decision-02: dropping force is safe; the only real blocker is OfflineCapableFetcher's header-less cache-hit response.".
<#entry-task-09-drop-store-force-fetch-decision-02> schema:text "Drop force: true at both call sites in Store.fetch (main fetch + describedby auto-fetch) — rdflib 2.4.1 already carries the PR #871 fix, so the session tap's flagAuthorizationMetadata() is the working invalidation boundary; no shim needed. Supersedes decision-01.".
<#task-09-drop-store-force-fetch> dct:modified "2026-10-20T18:28:00Z"^^xsd:dateTime.
<#entry-task-05-mention-suggestions-from-search-and-store-decision-06> a schema:Comment;
    schema:text "Mention cycle 1 seam (Angelo confirmed, 2026-10-20): test at the mention() extension level, not extension-manager level — Tiptap Mention extensions are name-keyed, so a bare mention() has no separate suggestion.config; the public seam is mention(os).options.suggestion.items. The items function receives { query } and resolves [{id, label}] from the zero-arg buildSearchIndex() demand API and os.store.get(ref).label().";
    prov:wasAttributedTo <https://angelo.veltens.org/profile/card#me>;
    dct:created "2026-10-20T19:53:00Z"^^xsd:dateTime.
<#entry-task-05-mention-suggestions-from-search-and-store-note-02> a schema:Comment;
    schema:text "Cycles 1–3 (2026-10-20, TDD via wallaby): (1) mention(os) items delegation — items resolves search refs to {id, label} via store.get(ref).label(), empty when no os is given (2 tests, seeded red, green via wallaby; note: TS3919 blocks the first test from an async function, pinned with @ts-ignore per existing RichEditor.spec pattern). (2) mention() re-registered in RichEditor and the 3 skipped tests un-skipped (red confirmed via wallaby, then green). (3) RichEditor wiring: new optional os param passed to mention(os); wiring test asserts the registered mention extension's items() calls buildSearchIndex on the injected os.";
    prov:wasAttributedTo <../agents.ttl#llm-claude-sonnet-4.5>;
    dct:created "2026-10-20T19:53:00Z"^^xsd:dateTime.
<#entry-task-05-mention-suggestions-from-search-and-store-note-03> a schema:Comment;
    schema:text "Cycle 4 process note (2026-10-20): the first component implementation awaited usePodOS in componentDidLoad, which broke 11 existing pos-markdown-document tests — the editor must keep constructing synchronously (design principle from the reverted attempt, note-01). Angelo ruled (chose 'B', 2026-10-20): pass the PodOS promise straight through usePodOS → RichEditor → mention; the extension awaits it lazily on the first suggestion request. The old-a99f603c tip-tap suggestion items name probe (items.name === 'items') surfaced the stale-extension trap: the original items.ts must be overridden per mention() invocation.";
    prov:wasAttributedTo <https://angelo.veltens.org/profile/card#me>, <../agents.ttl#llm-claude-sonnet-4.5>;
    dct:created "2026-10-20T19:53:00Z"^^xsd:dateTime.
<#entry-task-05-mention-suggestions-from-search-and-store-decision-07> a schema:Comment;
    schema:text "Integration test for the mentions chain renders the BUILT custom elements (integration-dom runs against dist/ via loader's defineCustomElements(), so component source cannot be imported there — @Element() decorators are undefined). Test asserts via DOM (render <pos-app><pos-markdown-document editable file=...>, click edit, type into the ProseMirror element, expect the pos-mention-menu popup). Angelo stopped the trial-and-error here (2026-10-20); the test is written but not yet green — see note-04 for the remaining knowns.";
    prov:wasAttributedTo <https://angelo.veltens.org/profile/card#me>;
    dct:created "2026-10-20T20:05:00Z"^^xsd:dateTime.
<#entry-task-05-mention-suggestions-from-search-and-store-note-04> a schema:Comment;
    schema:text "Cycle-5 integration test (2026-10-20): green after two findings — (a) the built bundle must be rebuilt (npm run build) before integration-dom sees the new wiring, and the docs/elements readme churn from the build gets reverted before committing; (b) the menu popup mounts into document.body (tiptap suggestion default), not the shadow root, and the typed text must include the '#' trigger char — typing the query alone never activates the suggestion. Resolution: render pos-app + editable pos-markdown-document with a Blob-backed file, click the shadow-root Edit button, type '#test' into div.content .ProseMirror, expect exactly one document.body pos-mention-menu option carrying the real label-index label. Green via vitest (1/1) and wallaby full elements suite (784/784, 0 skipped). Note: wallaby must be restarted with the integration spec in scope (wallaby-skill stop, then run with the spec path) since the session excludes integration specs by default.";
    prov:wasAttributedTo <../agents.ttl#llm-claude-sonnet-4.5>;
    dct:created "2026-10-20T20:05:00Z"^^xsd:dateTime.
